  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual claim and visual subject",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the meme's textual material ('no one: steven hawking') and the visual material (steven_hawking) as the subject of the claim. The text positions Hawking as the sole exception, and the user, by consuming the meme, is implicitly identifying with the perspective of the text — that is, the user is projecting themselves as the 'no one' who can do something, while Hawking is the exception. This projection is onto the textual material which frames Hawking as the subject of the exception, and onto the visual material which represents him as the object of that exception. The user is not directly addressed by deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the meme format creates an implicit identification where the user sees themselves as the 'no one' and Hawking as the 'one' who cannot do it — thus projecting the user's self-positioning onto the textual and visual entities.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
  "extractedFrom": "94678",
